# Apache/LiteSpeed config for the cPanel docroot.
#
# This file lives in `public/` so `next build` copies it into `out/`, which
# means the cPanel deployment installs it like any other asset. Editing it by
# hand on the server would be undone by the next deploy.
#
# The site is a static export (next.config.ts: output: "export" with
# trailingSlash: true), so every route is emitted as `<route>/index.html` and
# the server resolves it from the directory with no help needed.
#
# Do NOT reintroduce the old rewrite rules:
#
#   DirectorySlash Off
#   RewriteCond %{DOCUMENT_ROOT}/$1.html -f
#   RewriteRule ^(.+)/$ /$1.html [L]
#
# They belonged to an earlier flat-file export (about.html, services.html, ...).
# Against the current layout they rewrite /about/ to a leftover about.html and
# shadow every real page, and `DirectorySlash Off` also stops /about from
# redirecting to /about/.
ErrorDocument 404 /404.html
